WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.647
The supplied fictional tabletop can help explain an

00:00:02.728 --> 00:00:05.793
intake design when its tests, ownership, and limits

00:00:05.828 --> 00:00:09.358
are visible. It has not established live integration

00:00:09.451 --> 00:00:13.154
or real customer outcomes. That limit is compatible

00:00:13.189 --> 00:00:16.684
with a clearly labeled tabletop explanation. It is

00:00:16.742 --> 00:00:18.762
incompatible with a claim that the service is

00:00:18.832 --> 00:00:22.390
ready for unrestricted live use. If a required

00:00:22.413 --> 00:00:25.316
approval step still fails, describing the limit does

00:00:25.362 --> 00:00:28.393
not make that criterion satisfied. Keep the issue

00:00:28.427 --> 00:00:31.934
pending and correct it. Explain one remaining limitation

00:00:32.003 --> 00:00:34.290
and why the stated use is appropriate or

00:00:34.348 --> 00:00:36.914
must be narrowed. Show how a person can

00:00:36.984 --> 00:00:40.464
review and correct the result. Save the READY

00:00:40.534 --> 00:00:46.246
review, corrections, final responsible statement, AI disclosure, and

00:00:46.327 --> 00:00:48.916
unresolved issues in the existing Project Record and

00:00:48.963 --> 00:00:52.887
workbook. Carry the same package into Lesson 6.4.
